From b3123c147c410cff9e24ed056d5bc2c380dd073f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slink <slink@local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:10:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] slink: version 4.6.1-slink3; the lossless entries honour the
 lower-case-names tweak (SlinkForkRevision=3)

The lossless (pureRGB) entries offered no misc tweak: every other tweak is a code
write. LOWER_CASE_POKEMON_NAMES is a data write over the species-name table, so a
lossless entry now offers exactly that one. It is applied as a byte transform in
place over every InternalPokemonCount row of the table (forms, spirits and
MissingNo have their own rows), mirroring RomFunctions.camelCase on the Gen 1
glyphs, written straight into rom[] so nothing is re-encoded; savePokemonStats
keeps skipping the name write on a lossless entry. The vanilla path is untouched.
Every pure section declares SlinkForkRevision=3 so the pipeline refuses a slink2
jar, which would silently drop the tweak in tweakForRom.
